[h1]A little work. A little danger. A purse full of gold.[/h1]

Beyond the palace gates, someone always needs a message delivered, a monster
dealt with, or a brave soul willing to see what lies beyond the last watchtower.
Now your heroes have a place to find that work.

[b]Adventurers Guild[/b] brings a new gathering place to your kingdom: a
quest board full of opportunities, chosen and completed by the heroes themselves.
They take a job, head out into the world, and come home to collect their pay.

[h2]Adventure comes in all sizes[/h2]

Carry royal dispatches and collect supplies. Scout hidden lairs, chart the
wilderness, and seek lost treasure. Hunt dangerous monsters, clear troublesome
pests, answer reward flags, or help bring down a hostile den.

Not every job calls for a lone adventurer. Support another hero, escort a
caravan, patrol your defenses, stand guard, try your luck in a tournament,
survey a trade route, or put those potions to practical use.

[b]Sixteen quest types[/b] give your heroes new ways to earn a little more
coin for life's necessities. Better weapons. Better armor. Perhaps a potion
they really should have bought before leaving town.

[h2]Your doors, your decision[/h2]

[list]
[*]Build one Adventurers Guild per player for [b]3,000 gold[/b].
[*]It starts [b]closed[/b]. Open it when your kingdom is ready for questing.
[*]The board posts up to [b]six different eligible quest types[/b], depending on your map.
[*]Spend [b]500 gold[/b] to refresh the unclaimed jobs. Adventures already underway are left alone.
[*]Up to [b]four heroes[/b] can hold quests at once.
[*]An unfinished quest can return to the board if its hero dies and the remaining objective is still possible. The next Refresh replaces those offers too.
[/list]

Heroes remain heroes: independent, occasionally overconfident, and not always
ready to take the job you had in mind. Rewards are earned by doing the work
and returning to the Guild, not simply by watching someone else solve a problem
on the other side of the kingdom.

[h2]Requires Majesty Mod Manager 0.3.6 or newer[/h2]

Subscribe to this mod and
[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3793024054]Majesty Mod Manager[/url].
In the Manager, select Adventurers Guild under [b]Merge[/b], choose
[b]Prepare Selected Mods[/b], then [b]Launch Majesty[/b]. Continue launching
through the Manager when playing with this mod.

The Manager is also available through
[url=https://github.com/Phantomstar721/majesty-gold-hd-mod-manager/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url].
Keep only one installed copy of the Guild: Workshop or local, not both.

[i]The doors are ready. The board is waiting. All your heroes need is a reason to step outside.[/i]

